Chlorine undergoes the $simultaneous oxidationreduction. Chlorine is simultaneously reduced to chloride ion\left(\mathrm{Cl}^{-}\right)$and is oxidised to either $\mathrm{ClO}^{-}$ or $\mathrm{ClO}_3^{-}$ion. Halogens (e.g. Cl) have a strong tendency to accept electrons, so they act as strong oxidising agents.

